        "CommonSenseMedia": [
          {
            "id": 265028,
            "oneLiner": "Extremely violent sequel is sexist and dumb.",
            "AgeRating": [
              {
                "type": "official",
                "rating": 1,
                "age": 14
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "Review": [
          {
            "id": 148,
            "filter": "=148",
            "tag": "Nell Minow",
            "text": "Death by sequel. Extremely violent sequel.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.rotten",
            "link": "http://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/2-fast-2-furious",
            "source": "Common Sense Media"
          },
          {
            "id": 149,
            "filter": "=149",
            "tag": "Sara Michelle Fetters",
            "text": "Happily, those fears turned out 2 be unfounded as 2 Fast 2 Furious is far more entertaining then it has any right 2 be. It's 2 silly, 2 dumb and yet undeniably 2 entertaining 2 really care.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.fresh",
            "source": "MovieFreak.com"
          },
          {
            "id": 214,
            "filter": "=214",
            "tag": "Alex Pappademas",
            "text": "The vehicular action in 2 Fast is profoundly low-tech, and engagingly brawny.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.fresh",
            "link": "http://www.villagevoice.com/issues/0324/pappademas.php",
            "source": "Village Voice"
          },
          {
            "id": 144,
            "filter": "=144",
            "tag": "Richard Roeper",
            "text": "Director John Singleton once promised greatness with Boyz N the Hood. Here he's going through the paces with a story that was old by the second season of Miami Vice.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.rotten",
            "source": "Ebert & Roeper"
          },
          {
            "id": 215,
            "filter": "=215",
            "tag": "Kirk Honeycutt",
            "text": "Walker and Tyrese go for a no-frills style, giving the antiheroic protagonists solid emotional underpinnings before all the fancy driving gets started.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.fresh",
            "source": "The Hollywood Reporter"
          },
          {
            "id": 212,
            "filter": "=212",
            "tag": "Marc Savlov",
            "text": "It's all very nice to look at, sure, but pretty colors and molten intercoolers aside, 2 Fast 2 Furious is about as exciting as a Yugo in quicksand.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.rotten",
            "link": "http://www.austinchronicle.com/gyrobase/Calendar/Film?Film=oid%3a162047",
            "source": "Austin Chronicle"
          },
          {
            "id": 216,
            "filter": "=216",
            "tag": "Charles Taylor",
            "text": "It's a terrible movie, stuck in plot idiocies and big, noisy set pieces like a tire mired in mud.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.rotten",
            "link": "http://www.salon.com/ent/movies/review/2003/06/06/fast_furious",
            "source": "Salon.com"
          },
          {
            "id": 217,
            "filter": "=217",
            "tag": "Todd McCarthy",
            "text": "This John Singleton-directed sequel provides a breezy enough joyride,but it lacks the unassuming freshness of the economy-priced original.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.rotten",
            "source": "Variety"
          },
          {
            "id": 208,
            "filter": "=208",
            "tag": "Mike Clark",
            "text": "Just another retread.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.rotten",
            "source": "USA Today"
          },
          {
            "id": 206,
            "filter": "=206",
            "tag": "Ted Fry",
            "text": "For all its technical prowess, pretty-boy looks and fetishistic appeal, 2 Fast is often laid low by a leaden script and a couple of glaring casting blunders.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.rotten",
            "source": "Seattle Times"
          },
          {
            "id": 207,
            "filter": "=207",
            "tag": "C.W. Nevius",
            "text": "Nothing says summer film fun like explosions, guns and cartwheeling cars -- and that's all here.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.fresh",
            "link": "http://www.sfgate.com/cgi-bin/article.cgi?f=/c/a/2003/06/06/DD216495.DTL",
            "source": "San Francisco Chronicle"
          },
          {
            "id": 159,
            "filter": "=159",
            "tag": "Carrie Rickey",
            "text": "The pic is closer to the PlayStation experience of Gran Turismo than to a movie. This is not to say that it isn't fun, only to say that it is more about sensation than sense.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.fresh",
            "source": "Philadelphia Inquirer"
          },
          {
            "id": 210,
            "filter": "=210",
            "tag": "Jay Boyar",
            "text": "It's not every movie that would announce its shortcomings right in its title.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.rotten",
            "source": "Orlando Sentinel"
          },
          {
            "id": 209,
            "filter": "=209",
            "tag": "Jami Bernard",
            "text": "Without Diesel, there's not much gas, at least not from the nonvehicular elements.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.rotten",
            "source": "New York Daily News"
          },
          {
            "id": 213,
            "filter": "=213",
            "tag": "Bruce Westbrook",
            "text": "Even if you resist recklessness, these car catharses surge with noise, energy and adrenaline.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.fresh",
            "source": "Houston Chronicle"
          },
          {
            "id": 145,
            "filter": "=145",
            "tag": "Tom Long",
            "text": "A mediocre film that could have been much worse.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.rotten",
            "source": "Detroit News"
          },
          {
            "id": 776,
            "filter": "=776",
            "tag": "Lisa Kennedy",
            "text": "Even more of a joy ride than the original.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.fresh",
            "source": "Denver Post"
          },
          {
            "id": 7145,
            "filter": "=7145",
            "tag": "Paul Clinton (CNN.com)",
            "text": "It's pure formula from start to finish, but that was obviously the goal from start to finish.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.fresh",
            "link": "http://www.cnn.com/2003/SHOWBIZ/Movies/06/06/sprj.cas03.review.2fast/index.html",
            "source": "CNN.com"
          },
          {
            "id": 625,
            "filter": "=625",
            "tag": "Roger Ebert",
            "text": "It doesn't have a brain in its head, but it's made with skill and style and, boy, is it fast and furious.",
            "image": "rottentomatoes://image.review.fresh",
            "link": "http://www.rogerebert.com/reviews/2-fast-2-furious-2003",
            "source": "Chicago Sun-Times"
          }
        ],
